offs in topic decisions. No undeclared per-task veto threshold.\",\n        \"test_policy\": \"Selection uses validation only; freeze before a single held-out assessment. Historical completed test suites remain unchanged.\"\n      },\n      \"secondary\": \"Macro Logloss; every task AUC/Logloss and per-task deltas; measured model and runtime cost\",\n      \"dense_optimizer\": \"AdamW\",\n      \"dense_learning_rate\": 0.0001,\n      \"sparse_optimizer\": \"Adagrad\",\n      \"sparse_learning_rate\": 0.05,\n      \"gradient_clip\": 10.0,\n      \"gradient_clip_scope\": \"dense parameters only, following upstream split optimizer training\",\n      \"precision\": \"bf16 autocast; TF32 disabled; no torch.compile\",\n      \"history_policy\": \"official_offline\",\n      \"history_visibility\": \"Exact released prefix/action inputs. Delayed feedback may not be mature at prediction time; results only establish this offline benchmark.\",\n      \"drop_last\": {\n        \"train\": true,\n        \"valid\": false\n      },\n      \"full_validation_samples\": 2871767,\n      \"training\": \"scratch; official single-pass recipe adapted to DIN; sum four BCE unless declared training-loss hook\",\n      \"baseline\": \"Initial empirical reference: DIN local activation over item-field history with action values and four separate heads; field/task adaptation, not exact original DIN reproduction\",\n      \"research_goal\": \"Explore and validate mechanism-distinct unified modeling of multi-field user/context/target features and multi-feedback behavior histories. Develop representations and information flow that jointly support sequence modeling, feature interaction and task prediction under the fixed data and compute protocol.\",\n      \"architecture_search\": {\n        \"scope\": \"Whole-model design, including replacement of the initial network and all internal representations.\",\n        \"design_dimensions\": [\n          \"Representation units: fields, events, behavior groups, learned slots and target/task tokens.\",\n          \"Information flow: stacked interaction, layer-wise joint interaction, parallel exchange, learned routing or other testable unified structures.\",\n          \"History selection/compression jointly designed with target/context-conditioned retrieval.\",\n          \"Derived features computed from authorized inputs: field matches, behavior counts/composition, grouping and sequence positions.\",\n          \"Shared and task-conditioned representations, prediction readouts and registered training-loss mechanisms.\"\n        ],\n        \"lineage\": \"parent_trial identifies a comparison and evidence lineage; it does not require code or architectural inheritance. inherited_components may be empty when the whole model is replaced.\",\n        \"proposal_unit\": \"A coherent mechanism hypothesis can require several coordinated structural changes. Build that structure and plan component, replacement or factorial controls to identify where its value comes from.\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Select by the equal-weight validation AUC mean across click, cart, favorite and purchase; report macro Logloss and every task change. Use that same rule for checkpoints, parents, topic gains, merge eligibility and final selection. Evaluate mechanism support, nearest-work differences and measured cost; compare closest architectural alternatives and the initial reference.\",\n        \"fixed_contracts\": \"Available sample information, labels, data split, scoring, resource accounting and the frozen host training recipe remain shared. Internal architecture and readout design are candidate choices.\",\n        \"reference_use\": \"UniRank comparison methods provide inspectable design references and nearest work. Agents choose and adapt mechanisms from local evidence.\"\n      },\n      \"research_budget\": {\n        \"seconds\": 43200,\n        \"start_event\": \"new_campaign_started_with_verified_dataset\",\n        \"start_unix\": 1794198624.5008233,\n        \"deadline_unix\": 1794241824.5008233\n      },\n      \"test_policy\": \"closed during research; any final suite must be frozen before held-out scoring\",\n      \"source_sha256\": {\n        \"baseline.py\": \"f4b473cbacf60d72cff90f3721ad754dd617ee6065fe3fca2fc9cd4be2b25c36\",\n        \"train.py\": \"a313f015c9d03ae8244861bc36ff58517d8b630b968c397f404f627ea631522e\",\n        \"visibility.py\": \"d1f641c62fa3c72e1eadc03aad6d999cc9af87fceb783775eb22d1405d9ac6b4\",\n        \"data.py\": \"ef28cb65880b6931d3e567d2bfb4a67d7530c18067b68e47bf483b65b2560438\",\n        \"selection.py\": \"aa519982aebe726806e1d11b68fca2574d33993778c3392997843fe489fd9aff\",\n        \"selection-policy.json\": \"8e568c065a0412009879a3d42569e3469df6e6b81fb2837f94a1e04d39ffacf4\"\n      },\n      \"upstream_commit\": \"90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d\",\n      \"benchmark_deviations\": [\n        \"DIN is the initial empirical reference; unified research candidates can use entirely different architectures.\",\n        \"One GPU per model; batch8192 per model (single-device rather than published distributed global batch).\",\n        \"Validation selection uses the arithmetic mean of all four task AUCs; all tasks are reported separately.\",\n        \"Validation includes every sample; upstream default drop_last may omit remainders.\",\n        \"In-process DataLoader (num_workers=0): container shared memory is512MiB; all compared runs use the same loading policy.\",\n        \"No torch.compile; BF16; TF32 disabled.\"\n      ],\n      \"trial_cap_seconds\": 1208.5413760878146,\n      \"estimated_unit_seconds\": 483.4165504351258,\n      \"estimated_validation_seconds\": 75.56942507252097,\n      \"frozen_unix\": 1794198639.34825,\n      \"identity\": \"427fc51900560816321ba9bbc170639eb26625972df75b22e3c47d523c363748\"\n    },\n    \"method\": \"auto\",\n    \"budget_scope\": \"The research wall clock starts at protocol.research_budget.start_unix under its recorded start_event. Original acquisition uses verified download completion; an explicitly requested rerun on already verified data has its own fixed campaign start. Every later preparation step, calibration, agent call, failure, training/control and scoring job counts.\",\n    \"no_test_feedback\": true,\n    \"knowledge_revision\": \"knowledge-access-v3\",\n    \"knowledge_review\": {\n      \"policy\": \"Evaluate relevant external references against local evidence; adoption is optional. Missing source detail and negative transfer remain explicit.\",\n      \"proposal_output\": \"Add top-level knowledge_assessments: [{knowledge_id, decision: used|considered|rejected|unresolved, rationale, transformed_mechanism, variant_names, nearest_work_difference, falsifier}]. Cover retrieved industry cards; identify the concrete changed mechanism for used cards. This is provenance, not causal proof.\",\n      \"reflection\": \"Review the latest knowledge-usage.json alongside outcomes; distinguish declared use, executed changes, mechanism evidence and unresolved attribution.\"\n    },\n    \"latest_knowledge_usage\": null,\n    \"selection_policy\": {\n      \"id\": \"taobao-four-task-macro-auc-v1\",\n      \"split\": \"validation\",\n      \"tasks\": [\n        \"is_click\",\n        \"cart\",\n        \"fav\",\n        \"buy\"\n      ],\n      \"weights\": {\n        \"is_click\": 0.25,\n        \"cart\": 0.25,\n        \"fav\": 0.25,\n        \"buy\": 0.25\n      },\n      \"primary\": \"macro_auc\",\n      \"direction\": \"maximize\",\n      \"tie_breakers\": [\n        \"macro_logloss ascending\",\n        \"parameters ascending\",\n        \"trial_id ascending\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_task\": \"invalid; never average only the available tasks\",\n      \"regression_policy\": \"Report each task's AUC and Logloss change against the reference and entry model; explain trade-offs in topic decisions. No undeclared per-task veto threshold.\",\n      \"test_policy\": \"Selection uses validation only; freeze before a single held-out assessment. Historical completed test suites remain unchanged.\"\n    },\n    \"final_assessment_scope\": \"validation only; no test scores or predictions are supplied\"\n  },\n  \"study_schema\": {\n    \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n    \"title\": \"Task-independent prospective mechanism study\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"required\": [\n      \"id\",\n      \"protocol_ref\",\n      \"evidence_refs\",\n      \"question\",\n      \"hypothesis\",\n      \"nearest_work\",\n      \"inherited_components\",\n      \"proposed_difference\",\n      \"predictions\",\n      \"falsifiers\",\n      \"alternative_explanations\",\n      \"contrasts\",\n      \"cost_plan\"\n    ],\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"id\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"minLength\": 1\n      },\n      \"protocol_ref\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"minLength\": 1\n      },\n      \"evidence_refs\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"minItems\": 1,\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"question\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"minLength\": 1\n      },\n      \"hypothesis\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"minLength\": 1\n      },\n      \"nearest_work\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"minItems\": 1,\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"additionalProperties\": false,\n          \"required\": [\n            \"source_ref\",\n            \"verification\",\n            \"difference\"\n          ],\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"source_ref\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"verification\": {\n              \"enum\": [\n                \"discovered\",\n                \"read\",\n                \"archived\",\n                \"implementation_checked\"\n              ]\n            },\n            \"difference\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"minLength\": 1\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"inherited_components\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"proposed_difference\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"minLength\": 1\n      },\n      \"predictions\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"minItems\": 1,\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"falsifiers\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"minItems\": 1,\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"alternative_explanations\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"minItems\": 1,\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"contrasts\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"minItems\": 1,\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"additionalProperties\": false,\n          \"required\": [\n            \"parent_ref\",\n            \"intervention\",\n            \"control\",\n            \"held_fixed\",\n            \"remaining_confounds\",\n            \"decision_if_supported\",\n            \"decision_if_not_supported\"\n          ],\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"parent_ref\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"intervention\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"control\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"held_fixed\": {\n              \"type\": \"array\",\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"remaining_confounds\": {\n              \"type\": \"array\",\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"decision_if_supported\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"decision_if_not_supported\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"cost_plan\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"required\": [\n          \"estimate_ref\",\n          \"all_variants_counted\",\n          \"attribution_reserve\",\n          \"assessment_reserve\",\n          \"stop_rule\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"estimate_ref\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"all_variants_counted\": {\n            \"const\": true\n          },\n          \"attribution_reserve\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"assessment_reserve\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"stop_rule\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required_study_protocol_ref\": \"427fc51900560816321ba9bbc170639eb26625972df75b22e3c47d523c363748\",\n  \"reference_format\": \"Use allowed_observation_ids verbatim for local evidence. Descriptive references are accepted when they contain a complete known ID. Correct any previous_runtime_error before submitting; its failed costs remain charged.\",\n  \"action\": \"Read candidate.py and baseline_reference.py, diagnose an observed limitation, check primary nearest work, and implement a feasible candidate. Write proposal.json containing study (matching study_schema), parent_trial (existing trial ID), and variants (1-4 objects with distinct name, file basename ending .py, role candidate/control, config object, and note). At least one candidate is required. Add key ablations or matched controls for the claimed mechanism when feasible; reference existing matched trials as controls where justified. Each variant is a standalone module. Do not run training. New architecture choices come from evidence; industry cards do not mandate them.\",\n  \"candidate_api\": {\n    \"Model\": \"Model(feature_map, model_id=..., gpu=0, **kwargs) -> torch.nn.Module; optional MultiTaskModel utilities. forward(inputs) returns {label+\\\"_pred\\\": probability [B,1]} for all four tasks. Host places the module on the assigned GPU.\",\n    \"architecture_scope\": \"Whole-model design for unified modeling. Model need not inherit the initial reference, retain its pooling, or use separate task towers; representations, interactions, routing and readout can all be replaced.\",\n    \"lineage\": \"parent_trial records the empirical comparison and evidence lineage. A complete rewrite may have no inherited architectural components.\",\n    \"proposal_unit\": \"Coordinated structural changes implementing one coherent mechanism are allowed; isolate their effects through planned replacement, component or factorial controls.\",\n    \"meta\": \"Read-only UniRank FeatureMap: features (ordered specs, sources, vocab_size), labels, data_dir. Full framework reference files are available through tools.py.\",\n    \"batch\": [\n      \"inputs=(batch_dict,item_dict,history_mask,multi_task_history_masks)\",\n      \"batch_dict: categorical user/context features int64[B]; current labels and lookup metadata are removed by host\",\n      \"item_dict: item_id,cate_id,campaign_id,customer_id,brand,price_bucket,action, each int64[B,101]; last position is current target, preceding100 are pre-padded history\",\n      \"history_mask: float 0/1 [B,100]; four task masks: [B,100]; use only masked history\",\n      \"Target action is always zero (unknown/padding), never a current label. Historical feedback policy is frozen in protocol.history_policy.\",\n      \"Historical item_id is a previous advertisement ID. Shopping events used to create auxiliary labels are only matched by user/category/brand.\",\n      \"No raw timestamps, event-time deltas, raw user IDs, full future histories, current labels or global sample indexes are supplied to forward.\"\n    ],\n    \"t