{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 /workspace/tools.py resolve unirank-code:OneTrans && python3 /workspace/tools.py read unirank-code:OneTrans --find 'MixedMHA' --lines 55\"","aggregated_output":"/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n{\n  \"id\": \"unirank-code:OneTrans\",\n  \"title\": \"OneTrans benchmark implementation\",\n  \"kind\": \"benchmark_reimplementation\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/salmon1802/UniRank/blob/90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d/model_zoo/OneTrans.py\",\n  \"version\": \"git:90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d\",\n  \"content_read\": true,\n  \"read_scope\": \"Representative forward paths and structural definitions; no end-to-end reproduction of this method.\",\n  \"access_scope\": \"Full pinned benchmark source for inspection; not proof of equivalence to the original author method.\",\n  \"locators\": [\n    {\n      \"symbol\": \"OneTrans.forward\",\n      \"line\": 132,\n      \"end_line\": 172\n    },\n    {\n      \"symbol\": \"OneTransBlock.forward\",\n      \"line\": 219,\n      \"end_line\": 252\n    },\n    {\n      \"symbol\": \"MixedMHA.forward\",\n      \"line\": 287,\n      \"end_line\": 343\n    },\n    {\n      \"symbol\": \"MixedFFN.forward\",\n      \"line\": 376,\n      \"end_line\": 394\n    }\n  ],\n  \"scientific_status\": \"external_reference\",\n  \"local_reproduction\": false,\n  \"text_sha256\": \"9ecc65ce02a6985f5ac1793737ae978c14de0ed9bae10d56f1e786cfd6abb880\",\n  \"content_sha256\": \"9ecc65ce02a6985f5ac1793737ae978c14de0ed9bae10d56f1e786cfd6abb880\",\n  \"text_ref\": \"source-text://unirank-code:OneTrans\",\n  \"text_lines\": 394\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"unirank-code:OneTrans\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/salmon1802/UniRank/blob/90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d/model_zoo/OneTrans.py\",\n  \"version\": \"git:90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d\",\n  \"access_scope\": \"Full pinned benchmark source for inspection; not proof of equivalence to the original author method.\",\n  \"text_sha256\": \"9ecc65ce02a6985f5ac1793737ae978c14de0ed9bae10d56f1e786cfd6abb880\",\n  \"total_lines\": 394,\n  \"start_line\": 200,\n  \"next_line\": 255,\n  \"truncated\": false,\n  \"text\": \"200: \\n201:         self.mha_layers = nn.ModuleList([\\n202:             MixedMHA(\\n203:                 input_dim=input_dim,\\n204:                 num_heads=num_heads,\\n205:                 num_ns_token=num_ns_token,\\n206:                 attention_activation_type=attention_activation_type,\\n207:             ) for _ in range(num_layers)\\n208:         ])\\n209: \\n210:         self.ffn_layers = nn.ModuleList([\\n211:             MixedFFN(\\n212:                 input_dim=input_dim,\\n213:                 num_ns_token=num_ns_token,\\n214:                 dnn_activations=dnn_activations,\\n215:                 expansion_factor=expansion_factor\\n216:             ) for _ in range(num_layers)\\n217:         ])\\n218: \\n219:     def forward(self, s_tokens, ns_tokens, mask=None):\\n220:         if mask is not None:\\n221:             s_tokens = s_tokens * mask.unsqueeze(-1).float()\\n222:             q_mask = mask\\n223:         else:\\n224:             q_mask = None\\n225: \\n226:         ps_tokens = s_tokens\\n227:         for i in range(self.num_layers):\\n228:             # Prune sequence queries only. NS tokens stay in the separate\\n229:             # ns_tokens stream and keep a fixed token count across all layers.\\n230:             num_sequence_tokens = ps_tokens.size(1)\\n231:             sequence_start = int(num_sequence_tokens * self.reduction_ratio)\\n232:             ps_tokens = ps_tokens[:, sequence_start:, :]\\n233:             if q_mask is not None:\\n234:                 q_mask = q_mask[:, sequence_start:]\\n235:             norm_s = self.norm1_layers[i](s_tokens)\\n236:             norm_ps = self.norm1_layers[i](ps_tokens)\\n237:             norm_ns = self.norm1_layers[i](ns_tokens)\\n238: \\n239:             delta_ps, delta_ns = self.mha_layers[i](norm_s, norm_ps, norm_ns, kv_mask=mask, q_mask=q_mask)\\n240:             ps_tokens = ps_tokens + delta_ps\\n241:             ns_tokens = ns_tokens + delta_ns\\n242: \\n243:             norm_ps = self.norm2_layers[i](ps_tokens)\\n244:             norm_ns = self.norm2_layers[i](ns_tokens)\\n245: \\n246:             delta_ps, delta_ns = self.ffn_layers[i](norm_ps, norm_ns, q_mask)\\n247:             ps_tokens = ps_tokens + delta_ps\\n248:             ns_tokens = ns_tokens + delta_ns\\n249: \\n250:             s_tokens = ps_tokens\\n251:             mask = q_mask\\n252:         return ns_tokens\\n253: \\n254: \"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ll preserve g0’s summaries, feedback memory, interaction block, and prediction towers, then add a four-query retrieval branch using g1’s evolving reads, low-rank values, and terminal match prior. A zero-initialized residual will let the host check that it starts at the g0 function.\n\nThe four arms will compare adaptive matching, a uniform prior, rotated field assignments, and no prior. These controls will test the added branch and its routing rule separately. Archived benchmark code was available for inspection; the original INFNet paper text was unavailable, so novelty remains unverified."}}
