{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport ast, json, hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot=Path('/workspace')\nconfig=ast.literal_eval(next(n.value for n in ast.parse((root/'candidate.py').read_text()).body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets)))\nfixed=['protocol 427fc51900560816321ba9bbc170639eb26625972df75b22e3c47d523c363748', 'released inputs, official_offline history and four-label order', 'six item fields, action embedding, user/context embeddings', 'g0 relation/time summaries, counts, full rank moments, relation/content banks and factorized feedback path', 'g0 joint/separate FeedbackMemory, JointBlock and four original towers', 'host scratch initialization seed 20262027, one epoch, batch 8192, history 100, optimizers and sum of four BCEs', 'same new module shapes, initialization order, rank positions, low-rank values, zero-start output and prior scale 2.0', 'validation macro AUC selection with declared tie breakers; every task AUC/Logloss and measured costs']\nconfounds=['Single-seed validation adaptation and winner selection; source scores have no seed uncertainty.', 'Uniform and no-prior routes have fewer effective gradient paths despite equal nominal parameters and common forward work.', 'Fixed cyclic rotation can be partly compensated through learned shared Q/K; a null rotation contrast does not disprove same-field semantics.', 'The branch adds depth, task identities, event access, low-rank reconstruction and delayed gradient flow through its zero-start output; these are not separately identified by this round.', 'The g1 adaptation uses four task queries seeded by the g0 final token mean rather than the full g1 field stream; historical endpoints are not a complete representation-by-interaction factorial.']\nstudy={\n'id':'g1-t001-terminal-retrieval-compatibility-v1',\n'protocol_ref':'427fc51900560816321ba9bbc170639eb26625972df75b22e3c47d523c363748',\n'evidence_refs':['baseline-din','g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate','g1-r0004-match_terminal_only'],\n'question':('Does adding g1-style evolving task-query event reads and terminal target-field matching to the intact g0 representation improve validation macro AUC above both frozen source bests, especially g0 at 0.8301982212762624, and is any added value attributable to adaptive same-field routing rather than the extra retrieval branch alone? Observed source evidence: DIN 0.8099233880793816, g0 0.8301982212762624, g1 0.8192325306335276. g0 beats g1 on every full-validation task, but the architectures differ. g0 empty-history macro AUC is 0.7248235765734043 versus DIN 0.7268428930232654 and g1 0.7307799953736445, with only 13 buy positives among 6444 examples; this exploratory slice is not evidence of a stable mechanism failure. g0 history>64 macro AUC is 0.8528771120550432 versus g1 0.8417448005421858. Only these three committed trajectories are locally available; their unimported ancestors, failures and abandoned branches cannot be treated as local evidence.'),\n'hypothesis':('Implementation inspection shows that g0 compresses events into shared target-weighted relation/time and feedback memories before its one JointBlock; no final task-conditioned query returns to the uncompressed event stream. The committed g1 retains read-only event keys for two evolving-query reads and task-specific terminal low-rank value pooling with an adaptive bounded exact-match prior. A task query conditioned on the stronger g0 representation may retrieve complementary event evidence lost by shared signed-weight summaries. Preserve the complete g0 model and add a zero-start residual from this g1-inspired branch to each tower\\\\'s existing pooled-value input. Adaptive routing should outperform both frozen sources and the no-prior/uniform/rotated active controls if query-dependent same-field alignment adds utility in this tested implementation. This is a prospective compatibility hypothesis, not an established mechanism or verified novelty claim.'),\n'nearest_work':[\n{'source_ref':'g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Exact source SHA256 d01b0578075182b2281ad00dc6dd090a4a77c4d1c81576e41883b2bd4ca54923 verified locally. All representation paths, FeedbackMemory and JointBlock retained. Add direct task-conditioned access to the event stream after interaction; alter only the pooled-value slice per tower via a zero-start residual.'},\n{'source_ref':'g1-r0004-match_terminal_only','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Exact source SHA256 a330564ff642ea0eec4e9d7a967cc21754f260e04941acb787c02b9bfed6fde0 verified locally. Inherit shared Q/K across two evolving reads and terminal wide-value pooling, five positive-ID match channels excluding price/action, bounded scale-2 field-selected prior, rank embeddings, read-only events, low-rank reconstruction and nonaffine value normalization. Use four g0-conditioned task queries instead of reproducing the full g1 field-token stream; retain all g0 towers and add a zero-start output. No transferred g1 contrast or mechanism effect is asserted from its one imported score.'},\n{'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':'Archived primary text 1706.06978v4 read, including lines 271-277 on unnormalized local activation. Inherit g0\\\\'s signed unnormalized DIN summaries and raw static skip; supplement rather than replace them with task-conditioned normalized terminal reads. No exact original DIN reproduction claim.'},\n{'source_ref':'unirank-code:INFNet','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned benchmark source 90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d lines 123-219 inspected: task-mask sequence hubs and repeated aggregation/broadcast. We retain the g0 feedback/time memory but use read-only direct events and a terminal exact-match prior, without sequence broadcast. This is benchmark source inspection, not validation of the original INFNet method.'},\n{'source_ref':'paper:infnet','verification':'discovered','difference':'Registry provides original paper provenance only; tools.py read reports detailed primary text unavailable. Followed its explicit fallback unirank-benchmark-v2 and inspected pinned benchmark code. Original-paper equivalence and novelty remain unverified.'},\n{'source_ref':'unirank-code:OneTrans','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned benchmark lines 219-252 inspected: persistent sequence/nonsequence interaction with token reduction. The proposed branch has four task queries over a fixed read-only prefix; no progressive reduction or sequence update. Original-paper audit is incomplete.'},\n{'source_ref':'paper:dmr','verification':'read','difference':'Only the primary author README is authorized/available; its lines 4-8 warn that original behavior data have category/brand/type and no item. Do not infer original DMR mechanics or transfer its inputs. Current benchmark historical item IDs are real previous advertisements; no shopping-item or conversion-attribution input is invented.'}\n],\n'inherited_components':['All of the committed g0 model/configuration: embeddings, six static item fields, context, action history, DIN local activation, five temporal bins, seven relation groups, relation-specific full rank moments and content banks, factorized feedback path, joint/separate feedback memory, one JointBlock, raw skip and four Dice towers.', 'g1 shared normalized read Q/K, two evolving query reads with residual task mixing, positive-ID exact matching on item/category/campaign/customer/brand, fixed 2.0 additive prior, learned valid-rank positions, head-averaged wide-value pooling, low-rank reconstruction and nonaffine value normalization.', 'Frozen host training, data visibility, four-task scoring, resource accounting and validation-only feedback.'],\n'proposed_difference':('Append TerminalRetrieval only after g0 reset/initialization inside torch.random.fork_rng(devices=[]). It seeds four task states from the mean of g0 valid final tokens plus four learned identities, executes two dynamic shared-weight history reads with task mixing, then pools 112-wide item/action values with the same Q/K and a five-field terminal prior. Reconstruct through rank 32 and nonaffine normalization, then use a zero-initialized 112x112 output to add a per-task residual to g0\\\\'s existing pooled-value input; tower dimensions remain unchanged. All modules have identical shapes and initialization across adaptive/none/uniform/rotated arms, and all three prior tensors are computed in each arm. Cyclic rotation changes the field-weight-to-match-channel assignment without changing values, masks or matches. No internal match bias or reverse event write is added. Padded IDs are sanitized by inherited g0 code, target action stays zero, matching rejects zero/padding IDs, all-empty reads have a zero null, and zero-history updates are exactly masked to zero. Source AST comparisons confirm unchanged FeedbackMemory, JointBlock and all g0 representation helpers; host forward/backward gates remain pending.'),\n'predictions':[\n'Primary: hybrid_adaptive will exceed g0 0.8301982212762624 and g1 0.8192325306335276 on all-sample validation macro AUC; report macro Logloss plus signed AUC/Logloss changes for each of the four tasks against DIN and both sources, with no undeclared task veto.',\n'Adaptive-specific support requires hybrid_adaptive > hybrid_none and hybrid_uniform. Adaptive > hybrid_rotated would further support alignment of selected field weights to their own match channels; equal adaptive/rotated performance leaves that attribution unresolved.',\n'Any first-seed advantage is preliminary. Seek at least three host-authorized paired seeds for selected arm, g0 and the closest active control; use paired user-cluster bootstrap if supported by the authorized host interface, without treating impressions as independent.',\n'Exploratory slices use only predeclared history bins empty/1-16/17-64/>64 and positive-ID match occupancy absent/one/multiple fields. Report sample and per-task positive/negative counts, missing intervals and insufficient support; do not choose slice bins from validation outcomes. The new branch produces no direct evidence on empty histories.',\n'Analytic added dense parameter estimate is 47904 at value width 112, token width 32 and four tasks: total 33070309, dense 1277093, embeddings 31793216. All four arms should have the same parameter count. Measure training seconds, complete-unit wall seconds, inference latency/throughput and peak memory; runtime equality is not assumed.'\n],\n'falsifiers':[\n'Failure to exceed the stronger frozen g0 source is evidence against added predictive utility for this implementation, even if it exceeds g1 or DIN; it does not refute all possible representation/interaction combinations.',\n'If no-prior or uniform retrieval reproduces the adaptive gain, reject the adaptive-routing explanation; attribute the result to a broader retrieval/capacity/optimization alternative pending further controls.',\n'If cyclic rotation matches adaptive, do not claim identified field alignment. If repeat gains vanish or reverse, treat first-seed selection as unstable.',\n'If measured cost is dominated at comparable quality by a source or active control, do not claim efficiency or justified added cost. AUC gain alone does not prove an equal-compute advantage.',\n'Host initialization parity failure, unavailable-input dependence, nonfinite forward/loss/gradients, padding sensitivity, nonzero empty-history residual, or a hard resource violation invalidates that implementation before interpreting metrics.'\n],\n'alternative_explanations':confounds+['Encoded nonzero missing/OOV IDs can coincide; exact encoded equality does not prove entity identity.', 'Official_offline delayed feedback maturity and whole-window vocabulary/static-snapshot assumptions limit production interpretation.', 'g0 already encodes target relations and feedback/time structure; redundancy, interference or the task-seed mean bottleneck may erase a complementary signal.'],\n'contrasts':[\n{'parent_ref':'g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate','intervention':'hybrid_adaptive: intact g0 plus the complete g1-inspired task retrieval residual. Compare against both frozen source scores and DIN.','control':'Existing g0 exact source/config is the primary reference; g1-r0004-match_terminal_only and baseline-din are secondary source endpoints. Host preflight must compare inherited named parameters and predictions at initialization under paired seeds; historical endpoints do not provide a new factorial contrast.','held_fixed':fixed,'remaining_confounds':confounds,'decision_if_supported':'Promote only provisionally by the frozen validation rule, then prioritize matched active controls and paired repetitions before compatibility claims.','decision_if_not_supported':'Retain g0 as best supported; inspect whether any active control improves and whether cost, redundancy, interference or task-seed compression warrants one discriminating follow-up within reserve.'},\n{'parent_ref':'g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate','intervention':'hybrid_adaptive uses the learned field softmax to combine exact-match channels into a terminal logit prior.','control':'hybrid_none computes the same adaptive/uniform/rotated tensors and uses zero prior; all event reads, task mixers, low-rank values and residual capacity remain active.','held_fixed':fixed,'remaining_confounds':confounds[:2]+['This isolates terminal prior use conditional on the extra branch, not the utility of dynamic queries or all g1 components.'],'decision_if_supported':'A repeatable gain supports incremental utility of terminal matching over the active branch.','decision_if_not_supported':'Withdraw matching-specific interpretation; a shared gain can arise from extra event access or capacity. Reserve a static-query or parameter-matched g0-only adapter comparison if that shared gain is consequential.'},\n{'parent_ref':'g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate','intervention':'hybrid_adaptive selects match fields from the current task query using existing read Q/K.','control':'hybrid_uniform assigns exactly 1/5 to every match channel at the same fixed scale 2.0; same match inputs, modules, parameters, common forward operations and prior range bound.','held_fixed':fixed,'remaining_confounds':confounds[:2]+['Realized prior distributions/entropy differ by design; this is adaptive addressing versus generic match-count evidence.'],'decision_if_supported':'Treat query-conditioned addressing as provisionally useful; repeat paired against the strongest control.','decision_if_not_supported':'Prefer uniform if selected by the frozen rule and cost; do not claim adaptive selection is necessary.'},\n{'parent_ref':'g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate','intervention':'hybrid_adaptive aligns each query-selected field weight with its own exact-match channel.','control':'hybrid_rotated cyclically rolls the five softmax field weights by one before combining unchanged exact-match channels; entropy, range, nominal capacity and matches are preserved.','held_fixed':fixed,'remaining_confounds':[confounds[0],confounds[2],'Field coding correlations can make a rotated prior useful; rotation is a routing control, not a guaranteed destruction of all informative matching.'],'decision_if_supported':'Conditional adaptive>rotated support narrows the explanation to field-weight alignment; require repetition and report the semantic/control limitation.','decision_if_not_supported':'Retain the null/negative result. Do not infer semantic alignment from a gain over g0 or none alone.'}\n],\n'cost_plan':{\n'estimate_ref':'baseline-din: 329.1126111894846 complete-unit seconds, 293.065191924572 train seconds; g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate: 490.2475524395704 wall, 443.3547066003084 train, 37.640943586826324 inference, 33022405 parameters, 8081687040 peak GPU bytes; g1-r0004-match_terminal_only: 853.6963618397713 wall, 811.0805727243423 train, 33.065044328570366 inference, 32115012 parameters. Runtime estimate 483.4165504351258/unit, cap 1208.5413760878146/unit; 19787.07539176941 seconds remained at resolution. New branch uses only four sequence queries per read, but its runtime is unmeasured; estimate conservatively 650-1100 seconds per full unit, not a promised bound.',\n'all_variants_counted':True,\n'attribution_reserve':'First tranche is exactly four full-protocol arms, upper budget 4834.165504351258 seconds at the host cap, including controls. Reserve at least 3625.624128263444 seconds for g0 replay/preflight, static-query or g0-only active-capacity replacement and one discriminating follow-up if a promising but unsuccessful implementation merits it. All preparation, source searches, diagnostics, failures, retries and host gates are charged; no local training or installation. Inspect runtime ledger before each host job and shrink tranche if needed.',\n'assessment_reserve':'Reserve at least 7251.248256526888 seconds (six capped complete units) for two additional paired host-authorized seeds of selected candidate, g0 and closest active control. Include frozen g1 in comparisons; repeat g1 too only if remaining budget allows, otherwise explicitly record omitted source repetitions. Current phase has no evaluation launch interface. Later seed changes must use the host-authorized repetition interface, not model CONFIG. Freeze exact sources/configs/checkpoint hashes, selected candidate, source references, key controls, seeds and commands before final validation repetitions. Held-out testing is unavailable and must never be requested; no closed-assessment data enter open research.',\n'stop_rule':'Hard campaign limit 43200 seconds, fixed deadline 1794241824.5008233, per-trial cap 1208.5413760878146; never increase limits. Before a substantive host unit require preflight plus its capped cost and necessary assessment reserve to fit the current ledger. Stop on invalid contracts, unresolved execution state, hard limits or no useful admissible contrast fitting reserve. Unknown execution state does not authorize duplicate jobs. Select with equal-weight four-task validation macro AUC and declared tie breakers only. If no measured candidate improves g0, deliver g0 as best supported and record negative controls/failed implementations; exhaustion is not scientific success.'\n}\n}\nvariants=[]\nfor mode,role in [('adaptive','candidate'),('none','control'),('uniform','control'),('rotated','control')]:\n    file='candidate.py' if mode=='adaptive' else 'candidate_'+mode+'.py'\n    cfg=dict(config);cfg['terminal_prior']=mode\n    sha=hashlib.sha256((root/file).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n    variants.append({'name':'hybrid_'+mode,'file':file,'role':role,'config':cfg,'note':f'Prospective, untrained {mode} terminal-prior arm; source SHA256 {sha}. Same estimated 47904 added dense parameters and common forward computations in all four arms; effective backward cost can differ. Host must run same-seed inherited-weight/prediction parity against g0 before training, finite forward/loss/backward at frozen BF16, all-empty/zero-length/singleton/full/mixed histories, invalid-padding changes, target-action invariance, zero/padding-ID no-match checks and prior bounds/rotation/uniform behavior. Zero-initialized output blocks other branch gradients on the first step by design; after a host update or controlled nonzero output perturbation check active branch gradients and masking again. No local training or numerical results are claimed.'})\nassessments=[\n{'knowledge_id':'unirank-method-infnet','decision':'used','rationale':'Pinned benchmark aggregation and task-mask hubs were inspected as nearest work and provenance for the inherited g0 feedback memory; original paper text is unavailable. No local transfer claim.','transformed_mechanism':'Keep inherited feedback/time memory; add a separate read-only task-conditioned event path rather than adopting bidirectional hub broadcasts.','variant_names':[v['name'] for v in variants],'nearest_work_difference':'Four g0-conditioned terminal task queries and exact-match logit priors supplement the intact g0 representation; no gated broadcast to sequence events.','falsifier':'No gain over g0 or active branch controls, or gain explained by extra capacity/optimization, defeats the tested added-utility explanation.'},\n{'knowledge_id':'unirank-method-onetrans','decision':'considered','rationale':'Pinned mixed sequence/nonsequence forward was inspected; full event-stream mixing and progressive reduction would change cost and representation jointly.','transformed_mechanism':'No progressive pruning or whole-stream replacement adopted in this round.','variant_names':[],'nearest_work_difference':'Only four task queries perform extra reads; all g0 representations and fixed 100-event visibility remain. Original-paper equivalence is unverified.','falsifier':'If task-mean queries lose information that full stream exchange retains in a future matched-cost control, reconsider this constrained design.'},\n{'knowledge_id':'unirank-method-ultrahstu','decision':'unresolved','rationale':'Card was returned by the OneTrans search and reviewed as external context; no original primary-source audit or local effectiveness evidence.','transformed_mechanism':'No HSTU transduction, hybrid sparse attention or sequence update adopted.','variant_names':[],'nearest_work_difference':'Read-only exact-mask retrieval on the fixed short prefix; no claim against the original method.','falsifier':'A future primary audit and matched local control are required before any adoption or comparative mechanism claim.'}\n]\nproposal={'study':study,'parent_trial':'g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate','variants':variants,'knowledge_assessments':assessments}\n(root/'proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Wrote proposal.json:',len(study['contrasts']),'contrasts;',len(variants),'standalone variants')\nprint('Untrained source hashes:',{v['file']:v['note'].split('SHA256 ')[1].split('.')[0] for v in variants})\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
